  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "Using a combined deliberative-modelling framework with UK citizens, the study demonstrates that public support enables a 37% reduction in energy demand between 2025 and 2050, delivering 20% of the emissions abatement required for the nation's net-zero targets. The findings indicate that public resistance is not a key barrier, provided that policies ensure demand reduction options are both practical and equitable.",
      "why": "It refutes the common policy assumption that public opposition prevents aggressive demand-side energy interventions, quantifying the specific abatement capacity that socially acceptable demand policies can deliver."
